    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem**: `frai gate init --ci` was creating FRAI-SPEC.md but not the GitHub Actions workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`.\n\n**Root Cause**: The `--ci` flag was defined on the parent `frai` command, so Commander.js consumed it at the parent level instead of passing it to the `gate` subcommand. The gate action handler never received the flag.\n\n**Solution**: Modified the gate command action handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to manually extract flags from `process.argv` that come after the `gate` command. This bypasses the Commander.js parsing issue by:\n1. Finding the index of 'gate' in process.argv\n2. Extracting all arguments and flags after it\n3. Passing them to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Testing**: Confirmed the fix works by running `frai gate init --ci` in a test directory and verifying both files are created:\n- \u2705 FRAI-SPEC.md (created)\n- \u2705 .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml (created)\n\nThe frai-cli package has been rebuilt and the fix is ready to use.",
